<h2 id="tokenisation">Tokenisation of Money and Stablecoins: executive masterclass</h2>
<p>An executive masterclass for banking, payments and central banking leaders, with Prof. Dr. Selim Yazıcı (Istanbul University, co-founder of FinTech İstanbul), offered through the FinTech İstanbul Academy in partnership with Payments Innovation Consulting. It is the companion masterclass to the Springer book <a href="/publications/">"Tokenisation of Money: From Fiat Currencies to Stablecoins"</a> (July 2026), which the two co-edited, and is built on modules already delivered at the EBA Academy in Frankfurt and Paris and at Saïd Business School, University of Oxford.</p>
<p>Stablecoins, CBDCs and tokenised deposits are moving from pilot to mainstream, but board-level understanding is lagging the technology. The masterclass is the business and strategy view: what tokenised money means for revenue, risk and competitive position.</p>
<h3>What participants learn</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Tokenisation and the taxonomy of money tokens: crypto, stablecoins, CBDC, deposit tokens, tokenised deposits, e-money tokens</li>
  <li>Stablecoins in depth: how they really work, the stablecoin stack, hype and reality</li>
  <li>CBDC and the Digital Euro: the outlook for banks and merchants</li>
  <li>Regulation: the EU's MiCA, the US GENIUS Act, and what they mean for you</li>
  <li>Strategic implications: deposit flight risk, new revenue pools, who earns what</li>
  <li>Interactive workshop: what this means for your organisation in the next 12-36 months</li>
</ul>
<h3>Who should attend</h3>
<p>Banking and payments executives, C-suite and board members; chief digital and strategy officers and heads of innovation; treasury, risk, compliance and regulatory affairs leads; central bankers, regulators and policymakers; FinTech leaders, payment service providers, acquirers and advisers.</p>
<h3>Format</h3>
<p>Half-day executive briefing or full-day masterclass, in person, also bilingual (English and Turkish). Slides, case studies, interactive workshops and quizzes.</p>

<h2 id="open-banking">Open Banking masterclass</h2>
<p>"Open Banking: transforming banking and the financial industry" - a compact and in-depth masterclass, typically an intensive two-day course in person, tailored to the participants: what Open Banking is and why it is happening, its key elements (APIs and consent), implementation, business models and the consequences for banks and their customers, use cases, and the outlook from Open Banking to Open Finance and beyond. For senior management, product development, strategy, marketing, data services, retail and corporate services, legal and compliance, and IT in banks, regulators, FinTechs and service providers.</p>
